WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.590
Mirela Turulja calls it her dream job.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:10.059
For 12 years, she's worked in a state-run
home for the aging in Sarajevo, and she loves

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:15.990
it ... even though there are far too few staff
to take care of the 400 residents.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.769
Mirela regularly works over 11 hours a day.

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:25.269
She's highly qualified, but the job pays just
500 euros a month.

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:30.210
"You have to finish nursing school, and that's
not easy.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.840
And if you want to land a spot to study there,
you have to have excellent grades in school.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.030
Then the training program takes four years
to complete.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:42.870
Five actually...because when you're through
with classes you still have a year-long internship

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.070
and then final exams."

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.870
Because the training program they go through
is so rigorous, nursing staff from Bosnia

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.649
are also sought after in other countries.

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:57.250
Mirela says some colleagues work in Germany.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:03.600
But now a scandal has tarnished the country's
reputation for nursing excellence.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.120
Investigative journalist Azra Omerovic discovered
that several schools in Bosnia have sold diplomas

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.590
to people with no training at all.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.650
She uncovered the fraud by posing as an interested
client.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:21.320
"I called him and asked if he could help me
out with retraining.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:26.980
He said sure, and we met up the next day -- right
here, where we're sitting now.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:33.090
He told me to bring 2,500 Bosnian marks and
my school-leaving certificate, and that then

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.580
he'd be able to organize everything.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:42.430
It took exactly 17 days for me to get the
diploma after that first phone conversation.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:52.710
And I never set foot in a school, never mind
taking an exam of some kind."

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:58.080
Omerović and her editorial department secretly
filmed her interactions with the fraudster,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.140
and confronted him when he gave her the diploma.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.100
The employee in the area of public health
refused to name any backers.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:11.640
And so far, he hasn't lost his job.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.200
News like that makes Mirela angry.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.140
She knows better than anyone how even experienced
nurses can make a mistake -- with potentially

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.370
fatal consequences.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.220
Untrained staff who've bought their diplomas
could cause tremendous harm.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.740
"It's playing with people's lives!

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.860
This is a job with a huge amount of responsibility!

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.810
If you do something like that -- an unqualified
person taking responsibility for someone's

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.640
life -- I could never do that!

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.870
Why on earth would someone do something like
that?"

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:47.900
Azra Omerović and her colleagues discovered
the diploma she bought wasn't just a cheap

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.490
copy of a real one.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:53.680
It included certificates and documentation
backing it up.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.540
It says Omerović trained at a nursing school
for two years, and there were even records

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.510
of grades she supposedly got in courses.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:07.080
A foreign employer would never have been able
to determine it wasn't authentic.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:15.100
"I'm afraid the German authorities are going
hit the wall -- the wall of organized crime

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.100
in Bosnia-Herzegovina.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:24.280
If the Germans want to verify the diplomas
or the schools that issue them...or the people

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.680
that come to Germany with them to work...then
they're going to have problems with the relevant

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.980
Bosnian authorities.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.849
Why?

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:40.130
Because the Bosnian authorities are part of
the criminal system."

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:43.860
The scandal is a disaster for nursing schools
that play by the rules.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:49.560
The reputation for good work they worked hard
to achieve is being ruined by corrupt competitors.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.959
"This is pointless!

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:56.490
We study in this school for four long years
to take a diploma and hopefully find a job

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.750
in the field.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:03.860
Then they come and get the same thing in two
weeks.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:08.910
It just doesn't make sense!"

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:14.650
The police informed the state prosecutor's
office in Sarajevo about the case four months

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.650
ago.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.569
So far, it hasn't reacted.

00:04:17.569 --> 00:04:22.909
Politicians are demanding diplomas be examined
for authenticity, but not an investigation

00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:27.309
into the schools that issued them illegally.

00:04:27.309 --> 00:04:31.379
Mirela Turulja says she's never considered
taking a more lucrative position abroad.

00:04:31.379 --> 00:04:36.660
But for other graduates of Bosnian nursing
schools who dream of a job in Western Europe,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.609
the fraud has made landing one a much tougher
proposition.

